{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>תרומות</b> — three times in the Masorah: כל תרומות הקדשים · הרי בגלבוע אל טל ואל מטר ושדי תרומות · ואיש תרומות יהרסנה. This is what the Sages, may their memory be blessed, expounded: if a judge resembles a king who needs nothing, he sustains the earth — and that is ושדי תרומות, stated regarding Saul. And if he resembles a priest who goes around the threshing floors — and that is כל תרומות הקדשים יהרסנה (\"a man of terumot shall destroy it\")."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The three verses cited are Numbers 18:19, II Samuel 1:21, and Proverbs 19:26 (or 20:25, depending on reading); the latter phrase ואיש תרומות יהרסנה appears in Proverbs 20:25. The Masorah juxtaposition turns on the word תרומות appearing in all three."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:32.750922803Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}